ctive_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100446","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100446.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100446.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-09T16:34:41Z"},"body":"Build on top of #100440 \r\n\r\nI’ve only just started looking at these code, please point out if I miss something.\r\n\r\nA `VMap` provides array based ordered storage for a series of key-value pairs and offers a map-like interface. Currently it is only used in VisualShader code, and only three methods are used: `insert`, `has` and `operator[]`. It seems the user just want a normal `Map`. So I replace it with `HashMap`.\r\n\r\nPerformance wise `HashMap` should be faster (`O(1)`) compared to `VMap` (`O(log(n))`) theoretically, but I barely use visual shader and have no idea how to bench this.\r\n\r\nThis together with #100440 will obsolete `VMap`, shall we remove it or not? \r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{